---
import docs from "../../data/docs.json";
import site from "../../data/site.json";
---

<section id="menubar">
  <h2>Menu bar &amp; updates</h2>
  <p>Junction has no windows and no Dock icon. Click the menu-bar icon for:</p>
  <ul>
    {docs.menubarActions.map((action) => (
      <li><b>{action.label}</b> — <Fragment set:html={action.body} /></li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>Junction checks <a href={site.releases}>GitHub</a> for a new version once a day, and you can check yourself from the menu bar or <b>Settings → General → Updates</b>. It doesn't install updates itself: <b>Update to …</b> opens the release page, where you download <code>Junction.dmg</code>, drag Junction into Applications to replace the old copy, and clear the quarantine flag as on first install. Homebrew users can <code>brew upgrade --cask junction</code> instead of downloading (each release bumps the cask), then clear the flag the same way.</p>
</section>
